  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-m300.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-M 306.05 Request for Emergency Treatment Authorization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-M 306.05 Request for Emergency Treatment Authorization. A licensed practitioner shall submit, to the department of health and human service’s administrative appeals unit, a written request for emergency treatment authorization which shall establish the criteria enumerated in He-M 306.04 and which shall contain the following information:\n\n(a) A statement of facts demonstrating that a medical or psychiatric emergency exists, including the harm that would likely result from a delay in treatment;\n\n(b) A description of the patient’s admission status;\n\n(c) A description of the patient’s guardianship status;\n\n(d) A statement of facts demonstrating the patient’s lack of capacity to make an informed decision with respect to the medical or psychiatric treatment offered, including:\n\n(1) A description of the efforts that have been made to inform the patient of the nature, effects, and risks of the proposed treatment; and\n\n(2) A description of the treatment, if any, that the patient has agreed to accept and an explanation of why such treatment would not ameliorate the medical or psychiatric emergency; and\n\n(e) An explanation as to why a reasonable person would consent to the proposed treatment, based on its anticipated therapeutic benefit, the potentially significant risks, and the nature and severity of possible side effects.\n\nSource. #14637, eff 6-26-26, EXPIRES: 6-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-m300.html"
